---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
const updated = 'October 26, 2026';
---

<PageLayout title="Terms of Use" eyebrow="Legal" updated={updated} description={`The rules for using ${SITE.name}.`}>
	<p>By using {SITE.url} (the "Site"), you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.</p>

	<h2>Use of content</h2>
	<p>
		All articles, images, graphics and other content on the Site belong to {SITE.name} unless stated otherwise. You may read,
		share links to, and quote short passages from our content with a link back to the original article. You may not copy,
		republish or sell our content in full without written permission.
	</p>

	<h2>Information only</h2>
	<p>
		Content on the Site is for general information. It is not professional, legal, financial or tax advice. See our
		<a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Third party links and products</h2>
	<p>
		The Site links to third party websites, tools and services. We do not control them and are not responsible for their
		content, pricing, availability or practices. Your use of them is at your own risk and under their terms.
	</p>

	<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
	<p>You agree not to misuse the Site, including by attempting to disrupt it, scrape it at a harmful rate, or access it in ways that break the law.</p>

	<h2>No warranty</h2>
	<p>The Site is provided "as is". We try to keep information accurate and current but make no guarantees that it is complete, correct or up to date.</p>

	<h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
	<p>To the fullest extent allowed by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of the Site or reliance on its content.</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>We may update these Terms at any time. Continued use of the Site means you accept the updated Terms.</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
